[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: UAOP system requirements
UID: UAOP-SYS
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-21
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: ../02-standards/requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
What the system as a whole must do, allocated to the items of `system-architecture.md`. Each traces up to stakeholder needs (STK) or safety requirements (SAF). Software high-level requirements (`docs/lifecycle/05-requirements/hlr.sdoc`) trace up to these.

Active means some item implements it today, as read from the code; the COMMENT says where it is only partly met. Proposed means it is needed and not built. COMMENT names the product requirement in `docs/00_Project_Foundation/PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md` that the requirement restates, where there is one.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Vehicle state

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-001
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: MAVLink ingestion
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall receive MAVLink v2 telemetry from PX4 and ArduPilot vehicles over serial, UDP and TCP at 10 Hz full state per vehicle and at least 50 Hz for attitude.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-link
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-001. No vehicle link exists in the tree (PR-009).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-002
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Vehicle state machine
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall keep one supervised state per vehicle (disconnected, connected, ready, armed, in flight, landing, emergency) and publish every transition as an event.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-manager
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-002.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-003
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Link loss detection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall detect loss of the vehicle link within 3 s of the last heartbeat and show it on the station within 1 s of detection.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-link, gcs
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-004. The timeout logic exists only in the service template (`tools/service-template/src/domain/link_monitor.h`); see PR-012.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-004
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Staleness marking
STATEMENT: >>>
The station shall mark any displayed vehicle value as old when its source time is older than the staleness limit of its category, and when the stream reports a gap or stops.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gcs
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Simulation provenance
STATEMENT: >>>
Every event shall carry a flag saying whether it comes from simulation, the flag shall survive every stage, and the station shall mark simulated data on every display.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
ALLOCATION: contracts, gcs
COMMENT: The flag exists in the event envelope. The display part is not met: the station shows locally generated values with no marking (PR-001).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Telemetry subjects
STATEMENT: >>>
Telemetry shall be published on versioned subjects of the form `uaop.telemetry.v1.<vehicle>.<category>` and held in a persistent stream.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
ALLOCATION: contracts, bus
COMMENT: Contract and stream provisioning exist; no publisher yet.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stream to the station
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall stream telemetry and events to station clients in order per stream, with a per-stream sequence number, an explicit count of messages dropped by rate shaping, and a heartbeat at a fixed interval.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-008
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Source time reaches the display
STATEMENT: >>>
Every telemetry frame delivered to the station shall carry the time the data was produced at its source, unchanged by intermediate stages.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway, gcs
COMMENT: Not met: the gateway stamps frames with its own send time (PR-006).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-030
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Telemetry persistence
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall store all received telemetry at the received rate in the time-series store.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: telemetry-engine, storage
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-030. The schema exists; nothing writes to it.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-005

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Commands

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Closed command set, one vehicle
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall accept a vehicle command only when it names one vehicle and one kind from the closed set (arm, disarm, mode, return, take off, land, mission start), and shall refuse any other request.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: contracts, gateway
COMMENT: The vehicle identifier is not validated at the gateway (PR-010).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-005
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Command resolution
STATEMENT: >>>
Command submission shall return a correlation identifier at once, and each command shall resolve to accepted, rejected with a reason, or timed out; timed out shall be a distinct state shown as "state unknown".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: contracts, gateway, vehicle-manager, gcs
COMMENT: Contract and gateway forwarding exist. Nothing executes or resolves a command yet, and the station's own buttons bypass this path (PR-003).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-011
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Idempotent submission
STATEMENT: >>>
A command submitted again with the same idempotency key shall return the original correlation identifier and shall not be executed again.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway, vehicle-manager
COMMENT: The gateway forwards the key and does nothing else with it (PR-010).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Authentication
STATEMENT: >>>
Every interface other than health and login shall require a valid, unexpired, unrevoked token.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway
COMMENT: UAOP-NFR-010 in part. Met for the REST routes; not met for the WebSocket (PR-004). Login is a development stub (PR-007).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-013
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Role and controlling authority
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall admit a command only from a session with a commanding role that holds the single controlling authority for the vehicle, shall admit emergency-class commands from any authenticated pilot session, and shall record every change of authority.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: gateway, vehicle-manager
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-005, ADR-0017. No role check is applied today (PR-005).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-014
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Record before action
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall act on a command only after its audit event is durably stored, and shall keep emergency-class commands possible when the bus or the database is down by writing them to a local log that is reconciled later.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Analysis
ALLOCATION: vehicle-manager, compliance-engine, bus
COMMENT: ADR-0015.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-012
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-016
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Observer mode
STATEMENT: >>>
In observer mode the system shall receive a forwarded MAVLink stream or imported logs, shall hold no permission to publish on command subjects, and shall still produce capture, audit and evidence records.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: vehicle-link, bus
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-033, ADR-0023.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: No command without a person
STATEMENT: >>>
No item shall send a command, mission or parameter to a vehicle except on a request made by a person through the station or the gateway; analysis items shall have no path to the command subjects.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
ALLOCATION: flight-log, gateway
COMMENT: ADR-0012. Holds today because the analysis sidecar only reads events and writes reports.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-009
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-019
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Parameter writes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall check a parameter write against type and safe range, confirm it by acknowledgement and read-back, record old and new value with the actor, and show an unconfirmed write as a failure.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: parameter-engine
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-020, UAOP-HLR-021. Safe-range data exists in `backend/services/parameter-engine/data/`; no engine.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-020
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Mission and geofence upload
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall upload missions and geofences with retry, verify them by reading back what the vehicle holds, and record the content hash of each upload.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: mission-engine
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-010, UAOP-HLR-012.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Independence from the autopilot
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall hold no part of the vehicle's control loop, and loss of any UAOP item shall leave the autopilot flying and able to run its lost-link action.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Analysis
ALLOCATION: autopilot, procedure
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-011

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Records and evidence

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Audit chain
STATEMENT: >>>
The audit store shall be append-only with each entry holding the SHA-256 hash of the one before, shall refuse an entry that does not continue the chain, and shall deny update and delete to its writer.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Analysis
ALLOCATION: storage
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-042. Schema only; no writer or verifier yet.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-021
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Flight capture
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall capture each flight's log and record its content hash at capture.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Analysis
ALLOCATION: flight-log
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-032.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-022
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Evidence bundle
STATEMENT: >>>
For each captured flight the system shall produce a signed bundle that names by hash the log, the parameter snapshot, the analysis report, the pre-flight brief if any and the audit extract, and that verifies offline.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Analysis
ALLOCATION: compliance-engine, flight-log
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-044.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Post-flight analysis
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall analyse a stored flight log with a deterministic analyser, store the scored findings, and show them on the station.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: flight-log, gcs
COMMENT: UAOP-HLR-031.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Ordered, deduplicated events
STATEMENT: >>>
Every event shall carry a unique identifier and a per-source increasing sequence number; delivery shall be at least once, and consumers shall be able to discard duplicates and detect gaps.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: common, contracts, bus
COMMENT: UAOP-NFR-012 in part. Only an in-memory bus adapter exists for C++.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-005
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-028
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Evidence, not verdicts
STATEMENT: >>>
No display, report or bundle shall state that an aircraft is ready, airworthy, cleared, or go or no-go.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
ALLOCATION: gcs, compliance-engine
COMMENT: Not met by the station as built (PR-002).
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAF-013
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-006

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Platform

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Offline operation
STATEMENT: >>>
Every function shall work with no internet connection; a feature that uses a network outside the node shall be off unless configured.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Demonstration, Inspection
ALLOCATION: gcs, gateway, flight-log, bus, storage
COMMENT: UAOP-NFR-001.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Contracts only grow
STATEMENT: >>>
Interface contracts shall be defined once in `api/proto/`, versioned, and changed only by adding fields; a breaking change shall fail the build.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: contracts, tools
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-027
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Service health
STATEMENT: >>>
Each service shall report its health and metrics on a local endpoint and write structured log lines, so that a failed or degraded function can be detected.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: common
COMMENT: UAOP-NFR-004 in part. Nothing yet turns a failed health check into an indication on the station.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-029
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Errors by value
STATEMENT: >>>
Flight-influencing C++ shall report expected errors as values, without exceptions and without dynamic allocation on real-time paths.
<<<
RATIONALE: Makes every error path visible to review and test.
VERIFICATION: Analysis, Test
ALLOCATION: common
COMMENT: UAOP-NFR-008, ADR-0013.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-011

[[/SECTION]]
